WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.338
Set your ovens to hot and get
ready for some man-aerobics,

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.400
because we have the most
insane episode of "1984" yet.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.200
A lot of our theories have come true,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.420
so I'm here to break it all down and
what it could mean for episodes to come.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.220
You'll want to stick around to the very end to
see how this season could link to "Apocalypse".

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.640
Now let's get into it.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.440
Episode 4: "True Killers"
starts sometime in the near past

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.160
where Montana has a quick
pick-me-up before starting her class.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.560
We're at the Perfect 10 Aerobics Studio,
the same one we saw in episode 1.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.260
A not creepy at all Ricky Ramirez
watches from the window,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.820
and he either really
likes men doing aerobics,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
or something else has drawn him in.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:45.840
When he enters, it's almost as if a combination
of the music and Satan have led him to Montana,

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.940
who's quick to notice his knife.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.080
Ricky is training as well, just not his cardio.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.260
Montana steps into the locker alone, 'cause you know, it's man-aerobics and she's the only woman there.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:59.720
only to find the gutted
corpse of the Cyndi Lauper fan.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:04.220
And instead of screaming and running
the hell away, she is kind of turned on by it.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.120
Notice how he's strung up by these cords, the
same that can be found on Ricky's belt here.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.040
And Ricky goes to town on her feet.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.060
They engage in some post-coital pillow talk,
which includes arranging the murder of Brooke.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:26.980
And yes, as I predicted in my last video,
Montana is the brother of Sam,

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.640
the best man at
Brooke's ill-fated wedding.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.680
She believes Brooke lied about hooking
up with Sam the night before the wedding,

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.960
an event which caused
Joseph to kill him.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.100
Now she's hell-bent on revenge,
and Ricky is the one to do her bidding.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.960
Back in the present, Montana
chastises Ricky for not killing Brooke.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.640
Remember, he's had two opportunities
 to do it, and she's gotten away each time.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.800
She tells them that they have to
do it fast, since Jingles is around,

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.480
and then they'll make their escape.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.320
Trevor and Xavier have somehow
managed to get Chet out of that pit of spikes

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.260
and made their way back to the infirmary.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.620
Nope, no, he doesn't.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.560
After he passes out, they decide
to hit him with some adrenaline,

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.800
which apparently is
some really good shit.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.980
He tells them that Ray killed
someone in college and Xavier is like,

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.020
which reminds him that Blake's Cadillac,
that porn producer we met in episode 2,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.860
is still somewhere nearby.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.680
If they can get Margaret and Bertie and make
their way back to the car, they have a way out.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.760
So Trevor and Xavier decide to split up
and look for them, leaving Chet all alone.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.260
What could go wrong?

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:37.140
And I love how they just give Chet a pair
of scissors like, thanks ... thanks guys.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:41.625
Margaret finds the dead pranksters from
last episode, which really can't be good news,

00:02:41.625 --> 00:02:44.300
considering campers are
expected tomorrow morning.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:47.820
Trevor tries to get her to leave,
but she's gone full crazy and says

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.340
everything's gonna be
okay because she has a gun,

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.460
the same gun we saw at
the beginning of episode 2.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.240
Now when she touches the blood on
the body here, she gets a quick flashback.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.040
Is it from her surviving the massacre
or having done the massacre?

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.200
We'll get to that in a bit.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.880
Xavier heads over to the mess hall,
and bonus points if you picked up

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:09.180
that AHS alum Stevie Nicks
is playing on the radio.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:14.780
Bertie's there making sandwiches in the dark, because you know, that's what you do, when Jingles comes in.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:19.080
Xavier hides under the bench, and we
learn a little more about Margaret here.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.580
Bertie called her a "weird kid"
and says that she lives in the past

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:28.360
and wants to be here for Margaret to help
her turn the page with Camp Redwood's revival.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:33.660
Xavier is a total ding-dong and drops his
flashlight, alerting Jingles to his presence.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.400
Bertie tries to save them
but both are knocked out.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.480
And of course, it would be great if Xavier
revealed himself as Michael Langdon now

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.800
so he could survive the heat.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:46.600
Brooke wakes up in some sort of shed after
she was drugged last episode by nurse Rita.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:49.180
Or should I say psychologist Donna Chambers?

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:54.400
Remember that Rita and Jingles are working
together, and that she was instrumental in his escape.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.560
Now Brooke is able to
get out of the shed pretty easy,

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:59.640
but it doesn't take long for her
to spring one of those forest trap.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:04.860
Last episode, I predicted that it was Rita who set these up, since she would have had time, unlike Jingles,

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.400
to prepare the grounds
for their upcoming arrival.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:12.320
In episode 2 when Jingles visits her, she
would have likely told him where all the traps are,

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.140
so he could both avoid them
himself and capture more victims.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:21.460
Rita spills the beans and tells Brooke her
entire plan and uses Brooke as bait for Jingles.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:29.000
Will Jingles kill indiscriminately or
does he need the thrill of the hunt?

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.260
Last episode, we saw him leave the chubby
prankster when he could have easily killed him,

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.380
so his motives to
kill are still unknown.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.980
And rest in peace,
Xavier's beautiful porn career,

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:41.720
I swear if we have to watch Cody Fern with
blisters in his face for the next six episodes,

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:43.120
I'm not gonna be impressed.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.200
"Ma face!"

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.640
With her dying strength, Bertie
helps Xavier out of the oven,

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.220
and in an act of mercy,
Xavier puts her out of her misery.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.200
"Chef Bertie is good people!"

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:55.720
And great, his fingerprints
are gonna be all over that knife.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.660
Montana is outen aboot - yes, I'm Canadian -
looking for Brooke, when she finds her in the trap.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.080
Brooke tells her all about Rita, I mean Donna,

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.360
when Montana says to hang tight while
she gets her something sharp to cut her down.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.700
*cough, cough* Ricky.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.780
Margaret checks her gun,

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.820
when we're given this absolutely insane
flashback of her and Jingles from 1970.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:17.440
Notice the three counselors
here who make fun of her,

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.680
who are the same counselors
from the episode 1 massacre.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.940
She's given a bear carving by
Jingles as a symbol of strength,

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.560
then she goes on to say this weird
fact that bears mate for life, and

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.660
oh, oh god, what are you doing, please, no.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.400
Ricky makes a pentagram, seeking
guidance from the master, Satan,

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.480
when Montana directs
him where to find Brooke.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.500
Jingles arrives before
Ricky can touch Brooke,

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:46.220
and it seems as though he might have
a thing for saving defenseless women.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:50.400
But the most intriguing thing about this
scene is what Ricky says about the camp,

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.620
saying that the blood
spilled in this place is eternal,

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:57.420
and no matter which way you
slice it, Mr. Jingles lives forever.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.700
He's alluding to immortality, and
with his death through Jingles here,

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:04.060
and the fact we've seen characters
like the hitchhiker come back to life,

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:06.720
it's no wonder he comes
back at the end of the episode.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.440
During the scuffle, Rita and Montana
fight, and Brooke manages to get away.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:13.620
Margaret's here, praying for
Cody Fern to get his burns healed,

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:15.420
when she's confronted by Jingles.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:20.140
And we finally get confirmation
that she was the murderer all along.

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:22.560
We get this flashback
of Jingles being arrested

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.500
and his Vietnam ammo canister filled with
severed ears that were planted by Margaret.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:31.800
Here in Jingles' cabin, we can see her
plant the ears, which also includes her own.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.360
This bitch took off her own damn ear!

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.780
Also little thing, Jingles
also carved a cute bunny.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.140
(Chorus) Aww.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:41.480
Margaret proceeds to tell him the truth
about what happened all those years ago.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:45.960
The amount of drugs and electroshock
therapy he went through made him forget.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:49.240
He had promised to protect her
from the bullies but did nothing,

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:53.540
so she took matters into her own
hands - literally, by killing everyone,

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.580
making Jingles take the fall.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:07:00.120
Enraged by this revelation, Jingles
goes to kill Margaret but is shot by him.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.160
Remember what Ricky said: Jingles is eternal.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.600
Brooke, Trevor, and Chet meet up,
having heard the gunshots,

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.460
and for a guy who's
almost been killed a bunch,

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:13.640
he makes sure to tell Montana, who just rolled
around in the dirt fighting Rita, how gorgeous she is.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:17.220
What's going on, ladies, you are really
manipulating men this season.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:22.340
Although my favorite part of this scene is when Trevor tells Montana to take Chet, this bitch rolls our eyes!

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:26.440
Anyways, Trevor's off to look for Margaret
and - oh, oh no, this this can't go over well.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.860
Trevor sees that she's
killed Jingles, but it's too late.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:37.080
Margaret stabs Trevor,
having gone full psychopath.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:45.640
She takes off his ear, once again to
make it look like it was Jingles all along.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.060
And speaking of which, he's disappeared.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:51.880
As if Xavier night couldn't get any
worse, he stumbles into Jingles,

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:53.700
and his weak ass tries to stab him.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.700
But we get this line from Jingles,

00:07:57.340 --> 00:08:02.580
which could mean two things: either he's still
processing the revelation that he wasn't the killer,

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.360
or that it was actually Margaret
who stabbed Bertie to death

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.500
and threw Xavier in the oven
when they were both unconscious.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.880
I'll leave that one up
for you guys to decide.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:14.720
Brooke rushes in and Jingles has
once again mysteriously disappeared,

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.920
almost like he has some
sort of teleportation power.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:27.360
They see an explosion off in the distance, which we
find is their only means of escape: Blake's Cadillac.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.360
This is gonna be really tough to
clean up before the kids arrive.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:34.300
Margaret tells them that Jingles attacked
her and Trevor died in the process,

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:37.360
leaving the rest to process how
they're gonna get out of this mess.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:43.380
And now we have the coolest WTF moment of
the episode: the resurrection of Ricky Ramirez.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:50.860
Rita awakens from getting clobbered in
the head to find Ricky levitating in the air

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:52.920
and his wounds magically healing.

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:56.360
I don't know about you guys,
but I got some "Exorcist" vibes here.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:09:00.700
He looks as though he's possessed, you
can hear whispers of people saying "Satan",

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.480
and that combined with the levitation.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:07.740
But more interesting are his black eyes.
Now, where did I see that again?

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:13.000
I think this is huge proof that we're gonna see a bigger connection between this season and "Apocalypse".

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:16.820
And if there's a connection to "Apocalypse",
there's probably a connection to "Coven".

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:19.820
Now it's a bit too early to say
what exactly this connection is,

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:22.760
whether they are somehow
related or simply guided by Satan,

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.340
but it sure would have been handy for
Papa Satan to resurrect his own son last season.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:31.020
As with many AHS seasons,
a lot of it comes down to taste,

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:33.780
but this one is shaping up
to be one of my favorites.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.480
Let's hope Ryan Murphy
and the team can keep it up.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:41.440
Make sure to like and subscribe with the bell on,
because I'll be coming out with more AHS videos.

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:44.040
And leave a comment about what
you think about the season below

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:47.160
or send me theories
on Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.920
Until next time remember,

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.360
Daddy loves you very much.

